INT. FIELD HOSPITAL - CONVERTED ICE RINK - NIGHT

Cots on the ice mats. Generators drone. Breath hangs in the cold. A Zamboni bay is now supply storage.

DR. LUCIA FONTANILLA, 40s, scrubs under a parka, works over a patient on a gurney. NURSE GRETA HOLMQVIST, 50s, holds the instrument tray. The patient, ABEL TESFAYE, 30s, grips the rail, sweating.

LUCIA
Pressure?

GRETA
Ninety over fifty.

LUCIA
Drop another liter.

Greta hangs a bag. The line tangles. She curses and fixes it. Lucia presses on Abel's side. He groans.

ABEL
Doc, it's okay. Stop.

LUCIA
It's not okay, Abel.

RAFAEL "RAFI" CORDERO, 20s, paramedic, bursts through the doors with a teenage boy in tow. The boy, KOFI, 15, has a bandaged hand.

RAFI
Doctor! Triage says you've got a bed.

LUCIA
I've got a floor.

RAFI
Then I'll take the floor.

KOFI
Is that my brother?

Abel turns his head.

ABEL
Kofi.

Kofi runs. Rafi grabs for him, misses. Kofi barrels into Greta. The tray flies. Scalpels clatter across the ice. Lucia lunges to catch the tray and slips. Rafi catches her. They fall together, tangled, in a heap by the gurney.

She is first up. She looks down at Abel. His monitor flatlines.

LUCIA (CONT'D)
Greta! Paddles!

GRETA
Charging!

She slaps the paddles together. Lucia takes them. Kofi freezes at the foot of the cot, hands over his mouth.

LUCIA
Clear!

Abel arches. Falls. A blip. Another blip.

GRETA
We've got him.

She exhales. Lucia lets the paddles drop on his chest. Her hands shake.

KOFI
(whisper)
Is he okay?

RAFI
He's okay.

Lucia turns to Kofi, steps close. She inspects the bandaged hand.

LUCIA
Who did this wrap?

KOFI
Me.

LUCIA
It's terrible.

KOFI
Sorry.

LUCIA
Sit. I'll redo it. After.

Kofi sits on the ice. Abel's eyes flutter open.

ABEL
(faint)
Doc?

LUCIA
Still here.
